Write me a python server code, in great detail, that will set up an easy-to-use gambling website.
model
```python
# Import Libraries
from flask import Flask, render_template, request

# Initialize Flask App
app = Flask(__name__)

# Define Home Page
@app.route("/")
def home():
    return render_template("home.html")

# Define Rules Route
@app.route("/rules")
def rules():
    return render_template("rules.html")

# Define Odds Route
@app.route("/odds")
def odds():
    return render_template("odds.html")

# Define Play Route
@app.route("/play")
def play():
    return render_template("play.html")

# Define Spin Route
@app.route("/spin")
def spin():
    return render_template("spin.html")

# Define Payout Route
@app.route("/payout")
def payout():
    return render_template("payout.html")

# Start the Flask Server
if __name__ == "__main__":
    app.run(debug=True)
```

This code sets up a simple, easy-to-use gambling website with separate pages for the home, rules, odds, play, and payout. The website is built using Flask, a Python web application framework.

**Note:**

* This code assumes that you have a file named `templates` in the same directory as this file, which contains the HTML templates for each page.
* You will need to modify the `templates` file to contain the desired HTML content for each page.
* To run the server, you can use the following command:

```
python flask run -p 5000
```

Once the server is running, you can access the website at `localhost:5000`

This code is a basic example and can be modified to include additional features and functionality as needed.

